What are my goals?

The question: What determines the computational difficulty of breaking a cryptographic system, and how can that difficulty be reduced?

There are many different types of cryptographic systems of ranging complexity, so I will start simple and work my way up.
The different systems I want to investigate are:
- Caesar ciphers
- Vigenere ciphers
- Hill ciphers
- Substitution ciphers
- Toy Feistel/RSA

How can I measure the computational difficulty? Keep track of:
- Attack method
- Number of keys tested
- Time taken
- Ciphertext length
- Whether plaintext was recovered correctly
